//
// AN OPERATOR ON A STDLIB-DECLARED TYPE IS REFUSED (`@FR-Op-Std` crossed with `@FR-Op-Home`).
// Op-Std: "a type declared in `default/` keeps the stdlib's operator definitions … (Op-Home) binds
// the programs".  `Ordering` is an enum the stdlib declares in `default/01_code.loft`, not a type
// of this source, so a program's `operator plus(self: Ordering, …)` is refused at the definition —
// the stdlib type's operator table is the stdlib's alone.
//
// @falsified-at: none — a conformance guard; refused as the rule says, interpret and native.
// CHANNEL: the compile (the expected diagnostic).
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: the diagnostic names the stdlib type.
// HOLDS: `a-fn-named-for-an-operator-is-an-ordinary-function` beside it.
// @EXPECT_ERROR: `operator plus` defines `+` for a type of its own package, and `Ordering` is not one

operator plus(self: Ordering, o: integer) -> integer { o }

fn main() {
  println("x");
}
